# Generated by `pnpm run links`, which symlinks each of these to AGENTS.md. Two reasons they are
# build output rather than source: Git writes a committed symlink as a plain file containing its target
# path when core.symlinks is off (the Windows default), so the repository would ship a one-line file
# where the real instructions belong; and on a machine where symlinks are refused the fallback copy
# says so in its own header, which is true of that machine and of nobody else's.
CLAUDE.md
.cursorrules
.windsurfrules
.github/copilot-instructions.md
